WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.931
At just 21 years old, Daisy Ridley was far
from an established action hero when she was

00:00:04.931 --> 00:00:07.720
cast as Rey in Star Wars: The Force Awakens.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.350
In fact, she was all but unknown — her career
up to that point had been mainly minor roles

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:17.110
in small British productions, with no on-set
explosions or fight scenes to speak of.

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:22.000
So how did Ridley get herself in action-star
shape to join the sprawling Star Wars saga?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.010
Let's take a look.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.440
A lot of focus (and food)

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.039
Experts agree: when it comes to getting cut,
nutrition is far more important than exercise

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:32.010
in sculpting an eye-catching body.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:35.760
In Ridley's case, the already slim actress
wasn't trying to lose weight for her role,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.199
but rather bulk up to look strong and ready
to fight the First Order.

00:00:39.199 --> 00:00:40.379
"I had to put on muscle.

00:00:40.379 --> 00:00:41.909
So I was eating a lot.

00:00:41.909 --> 00:00:44.710
And I love to eat, but it got to a point where
I was like, 'I feel sick.'

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:48.670
But someone's telling you to eat, telling
you to eat, and you're just like, aggh."

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:52.579
But a high-calorie diet isn't a license to
eat empty calories like ice cream and drink

00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:55.589
beer all day — otherwise everyone would
be doing it.

00:00:55.589 --> 00:01:00.320
Instead, Ridley ate a healthy high-calorie
diet consisting of foods loaded with protein,

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.030
which is an essential ingredient to growing
muscle.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.610
Training as therapy

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:08.790
Ridley started her training just a few weeks
after she learned she got the role of Rey,

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.120
buckling down on a regimen of five-hour-a-day,
five-day-a-week workouts.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:17.000
Speaking to Elle, Ridley said she came around
to a mindset in which the lengthy workout

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.720
routines felt like more of a blessed oasis
in her day rather than an unwelcome interruption

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:22.720
in her life.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:23.720
"It became my solace.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.080
It's the only thing structured in my life
right now.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.500
Training is sort of a therapy session, I guess."

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.530
A combination of disciplines

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:34.750
While training for The Force Awakens, Ridley
chronicled her fitness journey on Instagram,

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:38.920
earning fans with popular "Fitness Friday"
posts that have since been deleted — but

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:41.790
live on through the archival efforts of her
online followers.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:45.530
In the videos, you can see her engaging in
a little bit of everything in the gym, from

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:49.240
resistance training to tone muscle, to core
strength-building workouts.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:53.800
She also engaged in activities as diverse
as kickboxing, rock climbing, and, of course,

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:54.920
tons of cardio.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:59.180
The end result of this variety of work is
overall fitness and a body that's generally

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:02.240
muscular, with no one muscle group exaggerated.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:07.250
After all, Rey isn't a musclebound warrior
— she's just a generally fit person, and

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.709
for the movie's sake, she needs to look like
it.

00:02:09.709 --> 00:02:11.170
Personal trainers

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:15.379
The main trainer Ridley worked with early
on was Jack Graves, a former rugby player

00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:19.040
— which may have something to do with all
the grueling cardio work that went into her

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.040
routines.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.209
But while Graves did the work for Ridley's
general fitness, she also worked with more

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:27.660
specialized trainers for activities specific
to Star Wars — like swinging swords around

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.049
in close-quarters combat, which saw her training
with a stuntman and choreographer who also

00:02:32.049 --> 00:02:34.819
helped design the fight sequences for The
Last Jedi.

00:02:34.819 --> 00:02:38.989
And Ridley told Vogue those lightsabers are
heavier than they look, weighing in at about

00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:41.739
ten pounds, so she really needed the conditioning:

00:02:41.739 --> 00:02:43.010
"They’re really heavy.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.510
[...] Three, four, five kilos?

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.750
And the weight’s very unevenly distributed."

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:48.650
A positive outlook

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:52.810
In one of Ridley's old Instagram posts, she
made a point about how what we see on Instagram

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:57.510
rarely corresponds to reality, and that her
fitness posts, while inspiring, hardly told

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.510
the whole story.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:02.340
"I have a trainer urging me on in workouts
and I don't include all the times I say 'I

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:03.340
can't do it'."

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.690
What she did include, though, was positivity
and excitement — an enthusiasm for the work,

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.569
even when she wasn't at her best.

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:11.189
As one characteristic post read:.

00:03:11.189 --> 00:03:13.299
"For anyone that's gonna try and correct my
form.

00:03:13.299 --> 00:03:17.349
I KNOW it isn't the best, I've just started
doing sprint training so progressing all the

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:18.349
time!"

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:21.750
This sort of positive outlook matters, as
does knowing that just because you're not

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.349
at your best right now, it doesn't mean you
won't get better.

00:03:24.349 --> 00:03:25.780
Thanks for watching!

